The dedicated suite compares the planning-HEAD dense reference and production
HiGHS solves on generated feasible, force-infeasible, torque-infeasible,
declared-wrench, cancellation, deterministic-repeat, and near-tolerance
systems.  Ten real-geometry fixture subtests cover balanced and one-ended
bars, offset stacks, counterweights, the drop/lift overhead couple, default
floor toppling, stability margin, a declared wrench, and exact support-edge
routing.  Comparisons include coefficient bytes after densifying the sparse
matrix, objective value, optimized per-row slack, targets, tolerances, ordered
body failures, and force/torque classification.

